{
  "title": "109: al-Kaaferoon الكافرون",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقُلْ يٰۤاَيُّهَا الْكٰفِرُوْنَۙ‏(1)\nQUL YAA AYYOHAL KAAFEROONA.\nSay, ‘O faithless ones!\nلَاۤ اَعْبُدُ مَا تَعْبُدُوْنَۙ‏(2)\nLAA A-A’BODO MAA TA’BODOONA.\nI do not worship what you worship,\nوَلَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عٰبِدُوْنَ مَاۤ اَعْبُدُ ۚ‏(3)\nWA LAA ANTUM A’ABEDOONA MAA A-A’BOD.\nnor do you worship what I worship;\nوَلَاۤ اَنَا عَابِدٌ مَّا عَبَدْتُّمْۙ‏(4)\nWA LAA ANAA A’ABEDUM MAA A’BAT-TUM.\nnor will I worship what you have worshipped,\nوَ لَاۤ اَنْتُمْ عٰبِدُوْنَ مَاۤ اَعْبُدُ ؕ‏(5)\nWA LAA ANTUM A’ABEDOONA MAA A-A’BOD.\nnor will you worship what I worship.\nلَكُمْ دِيْنُكُمْ وَلِىَ دِيْنِ‏(6)\nLAKUM DEENOKUM WA LEYA DEEN.\nTo you your religion, and to me my religion.’",
  "merits": "This Surah is ‘Makki’ and has 6 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that reciting this Surah carries the reward of reciting a quarter of the Holy Qur’an. The recitation of this Surah drives away Shaitan and keeps one safe from Shirk.\nIt is also among the five Surahs that have been recommended to be recited during a journey, the others being [Surah al-Nasr](A114), al-Tawheed, al-Falaq and al-Naas. Reciting Surah al-Kaaferoon and al-Tawheed in compulsory prayers is a means for forgiveness of sins for the reciter, his parents and his children. If a person dies after reciting this Surah, it is as if he has died a martyr. Recitation of this Surah before sleeping keeps one safe the whole night."
}
